From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:45:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 27/30] Require kernel process termination before supervisor
 acknowledgements

A successful runtime delete, or a missing workload, does not show that
the processes of a protected activation stopped. Both workers now keep
the exact activation they were started with and, when it is terminated,
pin the processes in the actor's cgroup, kill them, and wait until the
kernel reports each one reaped. Only then do they return an
acknowledgement. The kill is marked as deliberate first, so the crash
watcher does not report it. Tests run against a real cgroup and real
processes where the host is root, and otherwise check the binding rules.

Fork-Topic: supervisor-termination
Fork-Upstream: fork-only
